{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>His dwelling is the Elohim of old.</b> Know that מעון is like סוכה (booth), and the proof is \"and in Salem is His sukkah, and His dwelling-place in Zion,\" and many are like this. The meaning is: \"Your dwelling is the Eternal Elohim,\" like \"Elyon, You have established Your dwelling.\" You are a refuge for us. And the dwelling is above, over the one who shelters in it, while the place is below." "<b>And beneath, arms.</b> That they support you." "The meaning of <b>everlasting:</b> thus they shall be eternal and shall not weaken, and your dwelling shall not depart, for He is the Elohim of old, the meaning being קדמון (primordial), who has no beginning and end. And the meaning of \"beginning and end\" is relative to the created beings. The Gaon [Saadia] said that ומתחת means \"and beneath is HaShem,\" but he did not explain anything."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :register {:flags {0 ["the Eternal"]}}, :notes {2 "Resolved הגאון as the Gaon [Saadia] by inference from his known interpretation of this verse; the criticism \"did not explain anything\" suggests Ibn Ezra found Saadia's gloss insufficiently developed."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:26:41.005409789Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}